> f(x: u8) = [1,2,3][x+1]
> wrap f
wrap analysis of f:
  x + 1   (u8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=255
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=127
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 1 points, e.g. x=255
      exact for: 0..1
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range f
range of f -> int:
  1..3
  fits in u2
  undefined at 253 points
  over all 256 points of the domain
> g(x: u8) = [1,2,3][x]
> h(x: u8) = x < 3 ? [1,2,3][x] : 99
> equiv g h
g and h are equal on the domain of g (exhaustive)
> k(x: u8 in 0..2) = [1,2,3][x]
> m2(x: u8 in 0..2) = [1,2,3][x+1]
> equiv k m2
k and m2 differ at 3 points, e.g. x=0: 1 vs 2
> big(i: u32 in 0..1022) = [i, i+1, i+2][0]
> range big
range of big -> u32:
  0..1022
  fits in u10
  over all 1023 points of the domain
